 "about": "The Moon's ground round the base as a dimensioned plan the terrain stage (score/stages/terrain) makes into heights, in the base seat's flat numbers (x across, z along, metres, the base's middle at 0, 0). The flats, paths, craters and their settings are the plan the game 2099 laid its Moon with (its moonground jobs, 6 to 7 October 2026: BASE, PAD, SOLAR, DIG, STATION, PATHS and CRATERS); the old station's yard level and the wreck's dents are its ground record's (data/ground/moon.json); the garage's yard is new (the game's landed garage, ModuleRecord.LANDED at -17, 21 on the base seat, its 5 m big door in its south wall, an 8 m apron before it). The hangar's seat and yard are new (the captain's decisions, 2026-10-12): north of the greenhouse on its line, so the walkway tube from the greenhouse's north hatch to the hangar's south hatch runs straight (14.3 m), its south wall 4.3 m north of the habitat's north wall so the two clear; it is too long (46 m; 64 m since 2026-10-18, sized to the 46 m ship, its south wall kept where it was and its north wall 18 m further north, its yard grown to match) to stand on the ball's curve, so its seat is a flat plane touching the ball 4 m in from its south wall (its south end stands by the base's rooms, under the habitat's floor), and its yard is held 0.1 m under that plane (`on_seat`), rising to 4.4 m at its north-west corner.",
